// BitShop — PostgreSQL + Prisma (v8 — POS tenant + inventory integrity hardening)
// App Router / modular-monolith friendly schema.
// Prisma-only schema hardening. No SQL triggers, CHECK constraints, RLS, or custom SQL are assumed.
// Cross-row invariants (atomic stock, totals, default variant cardinality, workflow state) remain
// application-service responsibilities and are listed in the implementation notes.
//
// v4 CHANGELOG (everything below is ADDITIVE; no existing column was removed)
//   CASH REGISTER / SESSION
//     Terminal  = the cash register (till). CashShift = the cash session.
//     + Terminal.defaultOpeningFloat / hardwareConfig
//     + CashShiftCount   (opening / closing denomination count)
//     + CashShiftTender  (expected vs counted per payment method — card / transfer reconciliation)
//     + CashShift.differenceReason / differenceApprovedById
//   PAYMENTS
//     + SalePayment: customerPaymentId, receivedById, clientUuid, card info
//     + SaleRefundPayment (how a Return was actually refunded; split refunds supported)
//     + CustomerPayment   (lump-sum receipt that settles one or many credit sales)
//     + PaymentMethod: CHEQUE, STORE_CREDIT
//   PURCHASING
//     Purchase + PurchaseItem + (SupplierPayment + SupplierPaymentAllocation) already form the
//     "purchase payment" model; v4 adds Purchase.paymentStatus / amountPaid / returnedTotal,
//     PurchaseItem tax + discount snapshot, SupplierPayment.shiftId (paid from the drawer).
//   TAX / DISCOUNT SNAPSHOTS
//     + SaleTaxLine, SaleDiscountLine, SaleItem tax name/code snapshot, Sale.currency /
//       pricesIncludeTax snapshot, ReturnItem.taxRefundAmount
//   CREDIT / OUTSTANDING
//     + CustomerCreditEntry  (append-only receivable ledger)  -> Customer.creditBalance (derived)
//     + SupplierLedgerEntry  (append-only payable ledger)     -> Supplier.outstandingBalance (derived)
//   STOCK TRANSFER
//     + StockTransfer, StockTransferItem, StockTransferItemBatch  (shop -> shop, same owner)
//     + PurchaseBatch.sourceTransferItemId (traceability of received batches)
//   FINANCE
//     + ExpenseCategory, Expense.categoryId
//
// PRODUCT VARIANTS
//   Product        = shared info (name, description, brand, category, unit, image, tax rate)
//   ProductVariant = sellable + stockable unit (sku, price, reorder levels)
//   ProductBarcode = every barcode of a variant (a carton barcode may stand for N units)
//   A simple product has exactly one variant with isDefault = true and hasVariants = false.
//
// MULTI-TENANT ISOLATION
//   Shop-owned relations use composite foreign keys wherever Prisma can express them.
//   Optional tenant-owned links retain a required shopId and use a nullable parent id;
//   their onDelete behavior is RESTRICT to avoid SET NULL attempting to null shopId.
//   User membership/role authorization is enforced by the application service layer.
//
// STOCK — LEDGER + TRANSACTIONAL PROJECTIONS
//   InventoryMovement is the immutable business ledger. StockLevel, LocationStockLevel,
//   LocationBatchStock, PurchaseBatch.remaining and reserved quantities are projections.
//   Prisma schema can define tenant-safe FKs and idempotency uniqueness, but cannot enforce
//   aggregate sums, append-only permissions, atomic compare-and-swap, or transaction ordering.
//   Every stock write MUST run in one SERIALIZABLE transaction (or row-lock equivalent):
//   lock StockLevel + affected location/batch rows; conditional decrement available stock;
//   insert InventoryMovement; update all projections; insert/update reservation rows.
//   Retry serialization failures. Do not implement this as separate Prisma calls/transactions.
//
// MONEY MODEL OF A SALE (legacy POS module; unchanged in this inventory/website phase)
//   The previous application version documented trigger-maintained payment totals. This file
//   does not define SQL triggers; the application must own these updates if those migrations
//   are not deployed. Do not infer that Prisma schema alone maintains these totals.
//
// CREDIT MODEL (legacy customer receivable / supplier payable)
//   Ledger tables remain the historical source of truth. Balance fields are projections and
//   must be reconciled transactionally by application services in a no-trigger deployment.
//   Customer : +ve = customer owes the shop,  -ve = shop owes the customer (store credit / advance)
//   Supplier : +ve = shop owes the supplier,  -ve = supplier owes the shop (advance / over-payment)

generator client {
  provider = "prisma-client"
  output   = "../app/generated/prisma"
}

datasource db {
  provider = "postgresql"
}

